<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Losha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1374</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Losha was an Albanian clan leader who took Arta after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-orsini">Nikephoros II Orsini</a> around 1359. Recognised as despot by the Serbian ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-uros">Simeon Uroš</a>, he ruled the Despotate of Arta until his death in 1374, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjin-bua-shpata">Gjin Bua Shpata</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angelokastron">Angelokastron</a> and Lepanto to the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-losha.jpg" alt="Peter Losha" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Produced by Purger &amp;amp; Co., before 1905 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albania_Purger_13954.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
